<article class="env-lemma" id="06Y3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06Y3">Lemma <span data-tag="06Y3">15.60.8</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $K_1^\bullet \to K_2^\bullet \to \ldots $ be a system of K-flat complexes. Then $\mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits _ i K_ i^\bullet $ is K-flat. More generally any filtered colimit of K-flat complexes is K-flat. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Because we are taking termwise colimits we have 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits _ i \text{Tot}(M^\bullet \otimes _ R K_ i^\bullet ) = \text{Tot}(M^\bullet \otimes _ R \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits _ i K_ i^\bullet )  \]
</div>
    <p>
       by Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00DD" data-tag="00DD">10.12.9</a>. Hence the lemma follows from the fact that filtered colimits are exact, see Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00DB" data-tag="00DB">10.8.8</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>